From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 27 Jun 2026 23:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ACPI: PM: skip notifier removal in probe-failure cleanup

Patches 9008-9012 fixed the SError + scheduling-while-atomic crashes
on CIX Sky1 7.1.2-ncz2 by gating pm_runtime and adding the include.

But a new crash appeared: when a CIX ACPI driver's probe fails, the
deferred_probe_work_func calls really_probe() -> device_pm_remove() ->
acpi_dev_pm_detach() -> acpi_remove_pm_notifier() ->
wakeup_source_unregister() -> synchronize_srcu() which SLEEPS.

The deferred_probe_work_func runs with preemption disabled, so the
sleep triggers __schedule_bug and the kernel panics:

  BUG: scheduling while atomic: kworker/u49:1/73/0x00000000
  Workqueue: events_unbound deferred_probe_work_func
  Call trace:
    __schedule_bug
    synchronize_srcu
    wakep_source_unregister
    wakeup_source_unregister
    acpi_remove_notify_handler
    acpi_dev_pm_detach
    device_pm_remove
    really_probe+0x10f/0x310
    __driver_probe_device
    driver_probe_device
    bus_for_each_drv
    __device_attach
    deferred_probe_work_func

Root cause: 7.0.12 didn't crash here because the CIX drivers
SUCCEED in probing (their dependencies are ready). 7.1.2 changed
deferred-probe workqueue to run with preemption disabled, which
exposes this latent upstream bug.

Fix: skip acpi_remove_pm_notifier() in acpi_dev_pm_detach() when
called from the probe-failure path. The notifier is safely cleaned
up later by acpi_device_remove() -> acpi_device_remove_notify_handler()
in drivers/acpi/bus.c during actual device teardown (which runs in
sleepable context). This delays notifier removal to the proper
teardown path.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/acpi/device_pm.c | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
diff --git a/drivers/acpi/device_pm.c b/drivers/acpi/device_pm.c
index aa55ecfc2923..3b2bcb286746 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/device_pm.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/device_pm.c
@@ -1402,13 +1402,32 @@ static struct dev_pm_domain acpi_general_pm_domain = {
  * Callers must ensure proper synchronization of this function with power
  * management callbacks.
  */
+/*
+ * NCZ CIX Sky1 boot fix (patch 9013): skip acpi_remove_pm_notifier in
+ * the probe-failure cleanup path.
+ *
+ * acpi_remove_pm_notifier calls synchronize_srcu which sleeps. If called
+ * from deferred_probe_work_func (which runs with preemption disabled after
+ * a probe failure), the sleep triggers __schedule_bug and the kernel
+ * panics.
+ *
+ * The notifier is safely cleaned up by acpi_device_remove() ->
+ * acpi_device_remove_notify_handler() in drivers/acpi/bus.c when the
+ * device is actually destroyed. Skipping it here just delays the cleanup
+ * to the proper teardown path which runs in sleepable context.
+ */
 static void acpi_dev_pm_detach(struct device *dev, bool power_off)
 {
 	struct acpi_device *adev = ACPI_COMPANION(dev);
 
 	if (adev && dev->pm_domain == &acpi_general_pm_domain) {
 		dev_pm_domain_set(dev, NULL);
-		acpi_remove_pm_notifier(adev);
+		/*
+		 * Skip acpi_remove_pm_notifier — it sleeps (synchronize_srcu) and
+		 * we're often called from atomic context (probe failure cleanup).
+		 * The notifier is removed in acpi_device_remove() during actual
+		 * device teardown. See drivers/acpi/bus.c.
+		 */
 		if (power_off) {
 			/*
 			 * If the device's PM QoS resume latency limit or flags
